This allows scoring controls to remain visually distinguishable without making the admin interface excessively saturated.

---

# Score Changes

The current frontend score handler updates the relevant team.

A score cannot become negative.

Conceptually:

```text
newScore = max(0, currentScore + amount)
```

A corresponding score event is then added to score history.

This logic will eventually move into the Spring Boot service layer so that the backend becomes responsible for enforcing the rule.

---

# Custom Score Adjustment

The custom-score form allows the administrator to provide:

- Team
- Adjustment amount
- Reason

The form appears as a modal rather than permanently occupying dashboard space.

This keeps the main administration interface focused on frequently used controls.

---

# Score History

Score History displays scoring activity.

A score event currently includes:

```text
id
teamId
amount
reason
timestamp
```

The panel is intentionally constrained to a fixed/controlled size.

When the history becomes longer than the available space, the history area scrolls rather than continually increasing dashboard height.

The interface can also provide an expanded view for easier review.

---

# Add Team

Add Team opens in a modal.

This prevents the team form from pushing the rest of the dashboard down when opened.

The form receives the existing team list so that frontend validation can consider existing team information.

Backend validation will later become authoritative.

---

# Edit Team

Edit Team also opens in a centred modal.

The modal:

- Appears above the dashboard
- Uses a backdrop
- Remains within the viewport
- Allows vertical scrolling when necessary
- Adapts to smaller screens

The editing form receives the selected team and existing teams.

---

# Delete Team

Deleting a team uses a confirmation dialog.

The team is not immediately removed when the administrator first presses Delete.

The flow is:

```text
Delete
  |
  v
Confirmation
  |
  +---- Cancel ----> No change
  |
  v
Confirm
  |
  v
Team removed
```

This reduces accidental destructive actions.

---

# Undo Delete

After deletion, the application temporarily stores:

```text
team
original index
```

An undo notification appears for six seconds.

If Undo is selected, the original team object is inserted back into its previous position.

Only the most recent deletion is currently retained for undo.

The undo state currently exists only in memory.

---

# Reset All Scores

Reset All Scores is a high-impact administrative operation.

The interface therefore requires confirmation.

The intended flow is:

```text
Reset All Scores
       |
       v
Confirmation
       |
       +---- Cancel
       |
       v
Confirm Reset
       |
       v
All team scores = 0
```

Persistent auditing will be handled by the backend later.

