# Current Data Flow

The current frontend flow is approximately:

```text
App.tsx
   |
   |-- teams
   |
   |-- eventSettings
   |
   |-- scoreEvents
   |
   +---------------------+
   |                     |
   v                     v
Scoreboard         AdminDashboard
```

This means both public and admin views currently share the same React state.

That is useful because a score changed in the admin interface immediately affects the scoreboard within the same running application instance.

It does not yet synchronise separate physical devices.

---

# Future Data Flow

After backend integration:

```text
                Spring Boot
                    |
                    v
                PostgreSQL
                    |
          ---------------------
          |                   |
          v                   v
     Admin Device        Scoreboard Device
```

React will no longer be the permanent source of team and score data.

---

# Real-Time Requirement

One of the most important future frontend requirements is real-time synchronisation.

Example:

```text
Admin uses phone
      |
      | awards +10
      v
Backend
      |
      v
TV scoreboard changes
```

This must work even though the phone and TV are separate devices running separate browser sessions.

That functionality requires backend communication and has not yet been implemented.

---

# Frontend Error Handling

Once API integration begins, the frontend will need explicit states for:

```text
Loading
Success
Empty
Validation error
Network error
Authentication error
Server error
```

These should be designed intentionally rather than allowing failed requests to produce broken or blank interfaces.

